# Applied in order, with `patch -p1`, to an unpacked upstream Wine tree.
#
# Everything here is currently a *carried third-party fix*, not our own work.
# All four come from Debian's wine packaging and keep their original DEP-3
# headers naming their authors and upstream bugs. We carry them because
# upstream Wine 10.0 does not build usably on Debian trixie without the first
# one, and the rest are fixes we would otherwise hit.
# Our own patches live in patches/sg/, so "carried from elsewhere" and "written
# here" stay distinguishable at a glance -- which matters on a rebase, and for
# knowing whose authorship a hunk carries.
# We do not submit any of these upstream: Wine prohibits LLM-generated code, and
# David's decision is that we simply do not upstream. See ADR 0006. They are
# still kept small and one-concern, because that is what makes a downstream
# series survive rebasing onto new upstream releases.

